What is the documentation of First four 10GB port vs. the next 4o GB ports for Arista 7050QX-32S. How to make the 10GB ports to work. What configuration commands Arista needs to activate these ports vs. deactivate Ethernet5,please explain details.On the Arista DCS-7050QX-32S switch, the four dedicated 10GbE SFP+ ports (interfaces Ethernet1 through Ethernet4) are internally wired to share the same physical hardware lanes as the 40GbE QSFP+ Port 5 (interface Ethernet5).According to the official Arista documentation:Mutually Exclusive: You cannot use all of these ports at the same time. You must choose to activate either the four native 10GbE SFP+ ports (Et1-4) OR the 40GbE QSFP+ port (Et5).Default Behavior: By default, Arista EOS leaves the 40GbE port (Ethernet5) active. Consequently, the native 10GbE SFP+ ports (Ethernet1–4) will remain inactive and link-down until you modify the hardware port-group profile.Hardware Port-Group SelectionThe switch uses a global hardware layout command to route the internal Broadcom Trident II chip lanes to either the SFP+ cages or the QSFP+ cage.Desired ModeActive InterfacesDeactivated/Vanished Interfaces10GbE ModeEthernet1, Ethernet2, Ethernet3, Ethernet4Ethernet5 (Entirely disabled)40GbE Mode (Default)Ethernet5Ethernet1 through Ethernet4 (Entirely disabled)Configuration CommandsTo activate the native 10GbE ports and automatically deactivate Ethernet5, apply the hardware port-group mapping command.Step 1: Activate the 10GbE Ports (and Deactivate Ethernet5)Enter configuration mode and explicitly assign Hardware Port-Group 1 to select the SFP+ lanes:textswitch# configure terminal
switch(config)# hardware port-group 1 select Et1-4
Use code with caution.Note: As soon as you execute this, interface Ethernet5 will completely disappear from your running configuration, and Ethernet1 through Ethernet4 will become visible.Step 2: Bring the 10GbE Ports OnlineBy default, newly provisioned interfaces are administratively shut down. You must enable them manually:textswitch(config)# interface ethernet 1-4
switch(config-if-Et1-4)# no shutdown
switch(config-if-Et1-4)# exit
Use code with caution.Step 3: Save and Reboot the SwitchUnlike a simple speed change, hardware port-group mappings on this platform architecture require a switch reboot to re-allocate ASIC resources.textswitch(config)# write memory
switch(config)# reload
Use code with caution.Reverting Back to 40GbE Mode (Activating Ethernet5)If you ever need to restore the 40GbE Ethernet5 port and deactivate the 10GbE ports, use the following sequence:textswitch# configure terminal
switch(config)# hardware port-group 1 select Et5
switch(config)# write memory
switch(config)# reload
Use code with caution.If your 10GbE interfaces still won't establish a link after performing this reboot, let me know. I can help you verify your transceiver compatibility matrix, check for unsupported optic error logs, or configure a 4x10G breakout cable on ports 1 through 24 if you need more 10GbE capacity



